message.content:
Below is a minimal example of an **interactive rotating card** using only HTML & CSS (no JavaScript).  
When you hover over the card, it rotates around its Y‑axis.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="pl">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Rotating Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container ----------
   Keeps perspective so the rotation looks 3D */
.card-wrapper {
    width: 300px;
    height: 200px;
    margin: 50px auto;
    perspective: 800px;          /* depth of the 3D space */
}

/* ---------- Card ----------
   The element that actually rotates */
.card {
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    position: relative;
    transform-style: preserve-3d; /* allow children to be positioned in 3D space */
    transition: transform 0.6s ease; /* smooth animation */
    cursor: pointer;
}

/* Hover effect: rotate 180° around Y axis */
.card:hover {
    transform: rotateY(180deg);
}

/* ---------- Front & Back Faces ----------
   Both faces occupy the same space but are positioned differently */
.front,
.back {
    position: absolute;
    width: 100%;
    height: 100%;
    backface-visibility: hidden; /* hide the backside when facing away */
    border-radius: 10px;
    overflow: hidden;
    box-shadow: 0 4px 8px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    justify-content: center;
    font-family: Arial, sans-serif;
    color: #fff;
    font-size: 1.5rem;
}

.front {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #ff7e5f, #feb47b); /* front face gradient */
}

.back {
    background: linear-gradient(135deg, #6a11cb, #2575fc); /* back face gradient */
    transform: rotateY(180deg); /* start rotated so it's hidden initially */
}
</style>
</head>

<body>
<div class="card-wrapper">
    <div class="card">
        <!-- Front Face -->
        <div class="front">
            Front Side
        </div>
        <!-- Back Face -->
        <div class="back">
            Back Side
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
</body>
</html>
```

### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Provides a 3D perspective (`perspective`) so the rotation appears realistic. |
| `.card` | Holds both faces, uses `transform-style: preserve-3d` to keep child elements in 3D space. |
| `.front`, `.back` | Each occupies the same space; `backface-visibility: hidden` hides the side that is turned away from the viewer. |
| `.back` | Initially rotated 180° so it’s hidden until the card rotates. |
| `.card:hover` | Triggers the rotation with a smooth transition. |

Feel free to replace the text, colors, or add more content inside the `.front` and `.back` divs. Enjoy your rotating card!
